1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,899
MissionPay: Same vendor. Same treasury. Two outcomes.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:20,699
Live on Avalanche Fuji: Twin Treasury compares Global Allowlist vs Mission Guard.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Twin table: allowlist paid 0.01 USDC, mission reverted PayeeNotInMissionSet, 0 USDC lost.

4
00:00:41,551 --> 00:00:53,799
In Judge Mode, test any attacker: the contract strictly reverts with PayeeNotInMissionSet.

5
00:00:54,100 --> 00:01:18,299
Random attacker reverts with PayeeNotInMissionSet; owner proposal succeeds via eth_call.

6
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:41,299
Verify directly: copy cast call to query Fuji RPC. Note: updating root needs owner sign.

7
00:01:42,387 --> 00:01:55,000
Bounty Challenge: prompt injection fools the agent, but the contract preserves treasury.

8
00:01:55,299 --> 00:02:15,800
Tainted address from tool output is blocked by validator; contract provides hard backstop.

9
00:02:16,771 --> 00:02:26,800
On-chain proof: Snowtrace confirms execution reverted with PayeeNotInMissionSet.

10
00:02:27,352 --> 00:02:36,800
Independent verification: tamper with 1 single byte and the entire hash chain breaks.

11
00:02:37,098 --> 00:02:41,599
Dual-Layer Defense: LLM agents propose, while Avalanche Fuji contracts enforce.

12
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,800
LLMs can be fooled. Budgets on Avalanche can't.
